nodes.body:
Thanks for the ping @AndreasKaratzas! I took a look and the change itself looks good to me.

@Cross2pro, the red pre-commit is mypy complaining about the fake `ModuleType` in the test. Swapping the whole `vllm.platforms.rocm` module in `sys.modules` is a bit heavy-handed for what the test needs. If you move the `on_rdna4()` check into a small helper, the way `_rocm_torch_fp8_scaled_mm_supported()` already does it, the test can just monkeypatch that helper. I tried it on your branch and mypy, ruff and the tests are all happy.

One small thing while you're there: the reason ends up in the logs when the kernel gets skipped, and "not supported on RDNA4" reads as if it doesn't work at all. Something like "is slower than ChannelWise on RDNA4" would save the next person some head-scratching.

